-- A `fip` claim closes over the call tree per discipline. An `fbip` callee
-- certifies zero allocation only, so passing it an owned value leaves the
-- caller's linearity unproven and the claim is rejected; the fix the message
-- names is to certify the callee (`@ linear` or `fip`). (An `fbip` caller may
-- still call either discipline; the closure requirement is per claimed fact.)
fip fn use_it(x) = helper(x)

fbip fn helper(x) = x
